# cella.policy for build-pmars (titanium-owned: the task is vendored).
# The task builds pMARS from Debian source packages (apt over plain
# HTTP); the verifier bootstraps uv from astral.sh and GitHub releases,
# then pulls pytest from PyPI. Collected once with DRY_RUN=true, then
# reviewed: only the world names are kept -- the appliance's own infra
# (upstream DNS, the reply window, ARP) is composed by titanium, not
# declared here. The window keeps each flow live instead of freezing.
release outgoing deb.debian.org:80/tcp (keep_open=60m) (skip_freeze=true)
release incoming deb.debian.org:80/tcp
release outgoing astral.sh:443/tcp (keep_open=60m) (skip_freeze=true)
release incoming astral.sh:443/tcp
release outgoing releases.astral.sh:443/tcp (keep_open=60m) (skip_freeze=true)
release incoming releases.astral.sh:443/tcp
release outgoing github.com:443/tcp (keep_open=60m) (skip_freeze=true)
release incoming github.com:443/tcp
release outgoing release-assets.githubusercontent.com:443/tcp (keep_open=60m) (skip_freeze=true)
release incoming release-assets.githubusercontent.com:443/tcp
release outgoing pypi.org:443/tcp (keep_open=60m) (skip_freeze=true)
release incoming pypi.org:443/tcp
release outgoing files.pythonhosted.org:443/tcp (keep_open=60m) (skip_freeze=true)
release incoming files.pythonhosted.org:443/tcp
